ROUTE GROUP: /api/availability
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  GET /api/availability
  ─────────────────────
  Purpose: Return available booking slots for a given date
  Auth: None (public)
  Query params:
    date: string (ISO 8601, e.g., "2025-06-14")
    service?: string (service ID, for duration-based slot filtering)

  Logic:
    1. Call Google Calendar API to fetch events on given date
    2. Build an array of booked time blocks per staff member
    3. Load working hours from admin config (Google Doc or env config)
    4. Generate candidate slots (every 30 min within working hours)
    5. Apply 1-hour walk-in buffer to last hour of day (mark unavailable)
    6. For each candidate slot, check if any staff member is free
    7. Return available slots with assigned staff IDs

  Response 200:
    {
      date: string,
      slots: [
        {
          time: "09:00",
          available: true,
          staffId: "barber_kwame",
          staffName: "Kwame"
        }, ...
      ],
      fullyBooked: false,
      nextAvailable: null | string (ISO date if fullyBooked)
    }

  Response 200 (fully booked):
    {
      date: string,
      slots: [],
      fullyBooked: true,
      nextAvailable: "2025-06-15"
    }

────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ROUTE GROUP: /api/booking
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  POST /api/booking/initiate
  ──────────────────────────
  Purpose: Validate booking details and initiate payment step
  Auth: None (public, rate-limited)
  Body (JSON):
    {
      service: string,       // service ID
      date: string,          // ISO 8601 date
      time: string,          // "HH:MM"
      staffId: string,       // assigned staff
      clientName: string,
      clientPhone: string,   // Ghana format
      clientEmail: string,
      reminderMethod: "email" | "whatsapp",
      notes?: string
    }

  Logic:
    1. Validate all required fields (Zod schema)
    2. Re-verify slot availability (prevent race conditions)
    3. Calculate deposit amount (30% of service price)
    4. Generate a unique bookingId (UUID v4)
    5. Store booking in temporary pending state (see Pending Booking Doc)
    6. Return bookingId + deposit amount + confirmation to proceed

  Response 200:
    {
      bookingId: string,
      depositAmount: number,   // GHS, e.g., 45.00
      fullAmount: number,
      currency: "GHS",
      service: string,
      date: string,
      time: string,
      staffName: string
    }

  Response 409 (slot taken):
    { error: "SLOT_UNAVAILABLE", nextSlots: [...] }

  Response 422 (validation):
    { error: "VALIDATION_ERROR", fields: { ... } }

  ─────────────────────────────────────
  POST /api/booking/confirm
  ─────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose: Finalize a booking after payment verification
  Auth: Internal (called only after /api/payment/verify succeeds)
  Body:
    {
      bookingId: string,
      transactionRef: string
    }

  Logic:
    1. Load pending booking by bookingId
    2. Write full booking row to Google Docs log
    3. Create Google Calendar event with:
        - Title: "[Service] — [Client Name]"
        - Start/End: based on service duration
        - Description: client details, phone, payment ref
        - Calendar: per-staff calendar
    4. Mark pending booking as confirmed
    5. Return booking confirmation object

  ─────────────────────────────────────
  POST /api/booking/cancel
  ─────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose: Cancel an existing booking
  Body: { bookingId: string, reason?: string }
  Auth: Admin token or client email verification

  Logic:
    1. Find booking in Google Docs
    2. Delete Google Calendar event
    3. Update booking row status to "Cancelled"
    4. Notify client (email/WhatsApp) — non-refundable notice included
    5. Log cancellation with timestamp

  ─────────────────────────────────────
  POST /api/booking/reschedule
  ─────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose: Move a booking to a new slot
  Body: { bookingId: string, newDate: string, newTime: string }
  Auth: Admin token required

  Logic:
    1. Validate new slot availability
    2. Delete old Google Calendar event
    3. Create new Google Calendar event
    4. Update Google Docs row
    5. Notify client of change

  ─────────────────────────────────────
  POST /api/booking/waitlist
  ─────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose: Add client to waitlist for a fully booked date
  Body: { clientName, clientEmail, clientPhone, requestedDate, service }

  Logic:
    1. Append waitlist row to Google Docs Waitlist Sheet
    2. Send confirmation email to client
    3. When admin manually opens a slot: trigger /api/notify/waitlist-open

