4.1 PAYSTACK INTEGRATION
──────────────────────────
  Mode: Live (Ghana, GHS)
  API Base: https://api.paystack.co
  Auth: Bearer token in Authorization header (server-side only, never exposed to client)
  Secret key: PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY (env variable)
  Public key: NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY (safe for client if needed)

  Endpoints used:
    POST /transaction/initialize   → Create payment link
    GET  /transaction/verify/{ref} → Verify payment

  Amount handling: Paystack uses kobo (pesewas equivalent)
    GHS amount × 100 = pesewas value to send
    E.g., GHS 45.00 → 4500 in body

  Callback URL: https://yoursite.com/booking/confirm?ref={reference}
  Webhook URL (optional): https://yoursite.com/api/payment/webhook

4.2 GOOGLE APIS INTEGRATION
─────────────────────────────
  Auth: Google Service Account
  Scopes required:
    - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar
    - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/documents
    - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly

  Credentials: GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON (env variable, JSON string)
  Library: googleapis npm package

  Google Docs read pattern:
    1. Get document by DOCUMENT_ID
    2. Parse body content (paragraphs/tables)
    3. Extract structured data from table rows

  Google Docs write pattern:
    1. Use batchUpdate API
    2. Insert table row at end of booking table
    3. Use insertText or replaceAllText operations

  Google Calendar read pattern:
    1. events.list() with timeMin and timeMax for the target day
    2. Africa/Accra timezone always
    3. Loop through events to build blocked time blocks per staff

  Google Calendar write pattern:
    1. events.insert() on staff-specific calendar
    2. Set start/end in Africa/Accra timezone
    3. Populate description with structured client data

