SECTION 7 — ERROR HANDLING STANDARDS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  All API errors return consistent shape:
  {
    error: string,        // machine-readable error code (SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE)
    message: string,      // human-readable description
    details?: any         // optional extra info
  }

  HTTP status code conventions:
    200 — Success
    400 — Bad request / validation failure
    401 — Unauthorized (missing/invalid admin token)
    403 — Forbidden
    404 — Resource not found
    409 — Conflict (slot taken, duplicate reference)
    422 — Unprocessable entity (business logic failure)
    429 — Rate limit exceeded
    500 — Internal server error
    503 — External service unavailable (Google API, Paystack down)

  Error logging:
    - All 5xx errors logged to Vercel Log Drain or console.error
    - Google API failures: retry once with exponential backoff
    - Paystack failures: return 503 with "Payment service unavailable"
    - Never expose stack traces to client

